  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Nimoy is an 83-year-old man with COPD (GOLD 3, group B) who returns for his subsequent annual wellness visit, eight weeks after his six-month COPD review. His last annual wellness visit was with his previous primary care clinician more than a year ago. He completed the health risk assessment before the visit. He takes tiotropium-olodaterol two inhalations each morning and uses albuterol about twice a week, mostly before longer walks. He has had no flare-ups, antibiotic or prednisone courses, emergency visits, or hospital stays since his first visit in February. He keeps up the home exercise program from pulmonary rehabilitation, walking about 15 minutes twice a day and doing leg and arm exercises three times a week. He has no new concerns. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Subsequent annual wellness visit</td></tr><tr><td>Safety events</td><td>No falls, emergency visits, or hospital stays since February</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Tiotropium-olodaterol daily; albuterol about twice a week; no over-the-counter medicines or supplements</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>COPD, GOLD 3, group B, with no exacerbation this year; former smoker who quit about 30 years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent in all activities of daily living; walks about 300 meters before stopping; uses a wheelchair for long distances</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Fair; better since rehabilitation</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Lives with his spouse; close family and friends; enjoys his photography and writing projects; no loneliness</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Former smoker; no tobacco or vaping for about 30 years</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol and drugs</td><td>No alcohol (AUDIT-C 0); no other drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks about 15 minutes twice a day and does the rehabilitation strength routine three times a week</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular meals; weight stable; smaller meals when breathless</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours a night, sleeping flat on two pillows; no snoring or witnessed pauses reported</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent; showers seated on a bench to save breath</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Independent with medicines and finances; family drive him to longer appointments</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Single-story home; grab bars in the shower; smoke and carbon monoxide detectors working; no loose rugs</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>No falls this year</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Some difficulty following conversation in noisy rooms; reading glasses; eye examination last year</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>No concerns</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

