<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression, alcohol, cognitive, and fall-risk screens are negative. Possible hearing loss on the left on the whispered-voice test. [S]<list><item>Audiology for formal hearing testing.</item><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">COPD, GOLD 3, group B (J44.9)</content>. Stable on tiotropium-olodaterol, with no exacerbation this year and the gains from rehabilitation kept up. Resting oxygen saturation 94 percent. [S]<list><item>Continue tiotropium-olodaterol and albuterol as needed.</item><item>Influenza and RSV vaccines today.</item><item>Next COPD review, with yearly spirometry, in February as planned.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Former smoker (Z87.891)</content>. No tobacco for about 30 years. Not eligible for lung cancer screening, because he quit more than 15 years ago. [S]<list><item>No lung cancer screening; review only if the criteria change.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>High-dose vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Single dose given today; recommended for all adults 75 and older, and his COPD adds to the risk</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PCV20 given in May; no further doses needed</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at his age and with COPD; he will get it at the pharmacy next week</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two-dose series completed in the past</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap within the past ten years</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>More than 20 pack-years, but he quit more than 15 years ago, so he does not meet the criteria; he is also over 80</td></tr><tr><td>Abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>One-time ultrasound is recommended for men 65 to 75 who have ever smoked; he is 83, and no prior result is on file. Not offered</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Colonoscopy normal more than ten years ago; at 83 screening is a selective decision, and he chose not to continue</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not recommended after 70</td></tr><tr><td>Bone density (DXA)</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Evidence is insufficient for routine screening of men, but COPD and low activity raise fracture risk; ordered after discussion</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Universal one-time screening is recommended for adults 18 to 79; no risk factors</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0; PHQ-9 3 in February</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol misuse screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mini-Cog 5 of 5</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Timed Up and Go 11 seconds; no falls; home exercise from rehabilitation continues</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Referred</td><td>Whispered-voice test missed on the left; audiology arranged</td></tr><tr><td>Eye examination</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Eye examination last year</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: High-dose influenza vaccine, 2014-2015 season; RSV vaccine, single dose [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Global Strategy for the Diagnosis, Management, and Prevention of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease, 2025 report (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease monograph (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026); Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: COVID-19 vaccine at the pharmacy next week. Audiology and the DXA scan to be booked. COPD review with yearly spirometry in February. Next annual wellness visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
